hich extracts the `lint:` target body solely to assert two config-gate scripts appear — no bash-construct scan and no dash invocation","The `dash -n` language matches ticket 90c7-c465-4037-42d5's description ('a parse-only dash -n check does not catch set -o pipefail'), i.e. it is inherited framing rather than a description of the current module"],"finding":"The plan's rationale that test_ci_workflow_parity.py 'relies on parse-only `dash -n`' is not backed by the module: a Read of tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py (and a repo-wide search) finds no `dash` or `dash -n` check at all. The module executes workflow step bodies under `bash -eo pipefail` and does not scan make recipes for bash-only constructs. The gap the plan targets (no static bash-construct scan) is real, but the 'replace the dash -n check' framing describes a check that does not exist here.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1f34d7bff771164c","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context / Problem, item 2 (and Approach step 2 / Acceptance Criteria bullet 2): 'A parse-only `dash -n` check is insufficient because dash validates set -o pipefail at runtime, not parse time' and 'instead of relying on parse-only `dash -n`'","norm_id":"ne4ed6ff8cef234f1","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer reads AC bullet 2, searches the module for a `dash -n` check to replace, finds none, and is unsure whether the module under review is the right one or whether prior work was reverted"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Replace 'A parse-only `dash -n` check is insufficient because dash validates set -o pipefail at runtime, not parse time' with: 'The module today runs make/CI recipes under bash and never statically rejects bash-only constructs; because GNU make runs recipes under /bin/sh (dash on ubuntu) and dash validates `set -o pipefail` only at runtime, a static text scan (not a parse-only check) is required to catch it pre-merge.' Drop 'instead of relying on parse-only `dash -n`' from the AC.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Pin the derivation of the CI-reachable make-recipe set: enumerate the CI entry targets (`lint`, `typecheck`, `config-check`, `e2e-deps`) and follow the `$(MAKE) <target>` transitive closure (e.g. `actionlint-bin`), excluding dev-only targets, so the scan covers exactly the recipes CI executes.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_build-and-test.yml:102 `run: make lint`, :131 `make typecheck`, :137 `make config-check`, :507 `make e2e-deps`","Makefile:437 `$(MAKE) actionlint-bin` inside the `lint` recipe","Makefile dev-only targets (`worktree`, `hooks`, `install`) use `set -e` inside recipe lines by design"],"finding":"The plan does not define how the 'CI-reachable make recipe' set is derived, and the repo shows it is a nontrivial multi-root transitive closure: CI invokes `make lint`, `make typecheck`, `make config-check`, and `make e2e-deps`, and `lint` transitively invokes `$(MAKE) actionlint-bin`. Scanning only the three obvious targets lets `e2e-deps`/`actionlint-bin` escape; scanning ALL targets over-flags dev-only recipes (worktree/hooks/install) that legitimately use `set -e`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f19a0b70624c88500","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 / AC line 2","norm_id":"nc63b1ba623c24372","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer scans only lint/typecheck/config-check -> a bash-only construct added to the e2e-deps or actionlint-bin recipe votes green","Implementer scans every target -> the guard flags `worktree`/`hooks` legitimate `set -e` and blocks unrelated changes"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the make-recipe scan matches the Makefile-ESCAPED forms of each construct (e.g. `$${var^}`/`$${var,}` as well as `${var^}`), or normalize `$$`->`$` before matching, so a real recipe-level case-modification/here-string is actually detected.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3525,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'fail on non-POSIX-dash constructs: `set -o pipefail`, `[[ ... ]]`, ..., `${var^}` / `${var,}`'","Makefile recipes use `$$` to reach the shell (e.g. line 421 `[ -n \"$${GH_TOKEN:-...}\" ]`), so a shell `${var^}` is written `$${var^}` in the file","The check is a 'static text scan over every CI-reachable make recipe' — it reads Makefile text, not post-expansion shell text"],"finding":"Mechanism 2's forbidden-construct list is written in shell form (`${var^}`, `${var,}`), but the scanned material is Makefile recipe TEXT where a shell variable expansion is escaped as `$$` — a real case-modification appears as `$${var^}`. A literal-text scan keyed on the single-`$` shell form will not match the actual Makefile-escaped form, so the seeded defect could slip past.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8b7c0bf985ec4f2c","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 / AC line 2 (test_ci_workflow_parity.py static scan)","norm_id":"nc649adfcc9f3259c","priority":0.2475,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An author adds `x=$${