check.py exists but (search) scans standalone shell files, not make recipes — so shellcheck is available but not yet pointed at the CI-reachable recipe bodies the plan targets.","Retrieved shellcheck.net/wiki/SC3030 ('In POSIX sh, arrays are undefined') and SC3040 ('In POSIX sh, set option pipefail is undefined'): shellcheck's POSIX ruleset already covers the plan's enumerated construct list.","A hand-maintained regex list is a strict subset of shellcheck's maintained POSIX-portability family and will under-cover / drift as new bash-only constructs appear."],"finding":"Approach step 2 hand-rolls a fixed regex list for bash-only constructs and justifies it only against parse-only `dash -n`, without considering shellcheck — an established tool already vendored and pinned in this repo (`shellcheck-py` as a [dev] dependency; scripts/check_shellcheck.py) whose POSIX-sh mode already flags a superset of the same constructs (SC3040 `set -o pipefail`, SC3030 arrays, SC3010 `[[ ]]`, here-strings, case modification).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f340bf375aaead886","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 / Context problem #2 / AC line 2","norm_id":"nbd8fcdf0d433bb2a","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reachable recipe uses a bash-only construct the plan's regex list does not enumerate (e.g. `${var@Q}`, `${!ref}`, process substitution `<(...)`, `local` in some contexts) — the static scan passes it but dash would still fail at runtime.","The plan's regex for `${var^}`/`${var,}` or `[[ ... ]]` diverges from real recipe formatting and yields false negatives that shellcheck's parser would catch."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evide